  "job": "Hangs a healing lamp on the ally in the most trouble; the light follows them wherever they run.",
  "difficulty": 1,
  "lore": "In the Glass Belfry every window has a lamp, and Ilsheta was the girl who climbed the ladders to light them. When the morning stopped she kept climbing, because someone ought to. She hangs dawnglass lamps on people now: on runners heading out, on the wounded coming back, on anyone who looks lost. Aubade elders find her too gentle for the war. Serenade fighters find her lamps following them across the Noonline long after they thought they had escaped her. She is quick, tidy and never late.",
